.TH KEYLIGHT 1 "October 2026" "scripts" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
keylight \- cyclic keyboard RGB backlight profile switcher using OpenRGB
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B keylight
[\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR]
[\fB\-l\fR|\fB\-\-list\fR]
[\fB\-c\fR|\fB\-\-current\fR]
[\fB\-n\fR|\fB\-\-next\fR]
[\fIprofile\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBkeylight\fR is an automation utility designed for Linux workstations to manage and cycle keyboard RGB backlight profiles via \fBOpenRGB\fR.
.PP
By default, \fBkeylight\fR communicates directly with the background \fBOpenRGB SDK server\fR (\fB127.0.0.1:6742\fR) via a raw TCP socket, switching profiles in under 50 milliseconds without starting the heavyweight CLI. If the server is not running, it automatically falls back to invoking the OpenRGB CLI.
.PP
When invoked without arguments, \fBkeylight\fR sequentially cycles through declared illumination presets (\fBoff\fR \(-> \fBnight\fR \(-> \fBcyan\fR \(-> \fBwhite\fR).
A specific profile can also be activated directly by passing its name as an argument.
.PP
Active state is tracked locally in the user cache directory (\fB$XDG_CACHE_HOME/keylight-current-profile\fR), allowing reliable cyclic switching across multiple executions.
.SH HARDWARE CONTEXT & ARCHITECTURE
\fBkeylight\fR specifically resolves complex hardware limitations encountered on \fBMSI MS-1565\fR (Mystic Light) laptop keyboard controllers:
.TP
.B 1. Write-Only Controller (No Hardware Readback)
The MS-1565 embedded controller does not report its current color or mode back to the operating system. OpenRGB processes are transient CLI invocations that reinitialize hardware models on launch. Consequently, commands like \fBopenrgb \-\-save\-profile\fR record default uninitialized states (\fBOff\fR / zero colors), producing broken profile files.
.TP
.B 2. Multi-Zone Implementation Quirks
In the MS-1565 Linux driver, the keyboard's 4 physical RGB zones are implemented as mutually exclusive \fImodes\fR (\fBStatic zone 1\fR through \fBStatic zone 4\fR) rather than OpenRGB \fIzones\fR. OpenRGB profile JSON files only store a single active mode per device, making 4-zone lighting impossible through static configuration files.
.PP
To overcome these limitations, \fBkeylight\fR communicates directly with the controller via OpenRGB SDK network packets, pushing calibrated mode and color data with microsecond delays to prevent USB HID buffer saturation.
.SH PROFILES
.TP
.B off
Completely turns off keyboard backlight illumination.
.TP
.B night
Applies a gentle 4-zone emerald-to-olive forest gradient across the keyboard at 40% brightness:
.RS
.IP \(bu 2
Zone 1: Emerald (\fB#006644\fR)
.IP \(bu 2
Zone 2: Mint/Olive (\fB#006626\fR)
.IP \(bu 2
Zone 3: Forest olive (\fB#1E6610\fR)
.IP \(bu 2
Zone 4: Olive amber (\fB#386608\fR)
.RE
.TP
.B cyan
Static vivid cyan illumination across all zones (\fB#00FFFF\fR at 40% brightness).
.TP
.B white
Static clean, soft white backlight (\fB#FFFFFF\fR at 35% brightness).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Displays usage instructions, available profiles, hardware notes, and exits.
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-next
Advances to the next profile in the cyclic sequence (default behavior when run without arguments).
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-current
Prints the name of the currently active profile.
.TP
.BR \-l ", " \-\-list
Lists all available profiles with an indicator next to the active profile.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B OPENRGB
Path to the \fBopenrgb\fR binary. If unset, checks \fB$HOME/.local/bin/openrgb\fR, then searches \fB$PATH\fR.
.TP
.B XDG_CACHE_HOME
Base cache directory for storing current profile state (default: \fB$HOME/.cache\fR).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.cache/keylight-current-profile
State file holding the name of the active lighting profile.
